1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,340
What do you think you're doing?

2
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:14,320
You looked cold, so I thought I'd be an extra blanket for you.

3
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:15,760
Since I'm your familiar.

4
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,000
No, thanks!

5
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,940
It's been like this ever since she came here.

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,200
She's always glued to me at home.

7
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,140
Give me some space to be a man.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,620
Right, I have to take back control!

9
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,380
I'll teach her who's boss once and for all!

10
00:02:07,957 --> 00:02:22,357
The first step is to uncover her weakness

11
00:02:22,357 --> 00:02:23,177
Now then

12
00:02:23,177 --> 00:02:29,717
There's really no point in wearing clothes inside, you know

13
00:02:29,717 --> 00:02:32,017
What the heck is wrong with her?

14
00:02:33,217 --> 00:02:36,017
I'm so much more comfortable without anything on

15
00:02:36,017 --> 00:02:38,837
I suppose some might call that a shortcoming

16
00:02:38,837 --> 00:02:43,037
What is it, Chota Baby?

17
00:02:44,037 --> 00:02:45,217
This is for you

18
00:02:45,217 --> 00:02:48,337
Your master commands it

19
00:02:48,337 --> 00:02:49,837
Put some clothes on

20
00:02:49,837 --> 00:02:50,817
So awkward

21
00:02:50,817 --> 00:02:52,197
Is it over yet?

22
00:02:52,617 --> 00:02:54,337
I put it on for you

23
00:02:54,337 --> 00:02:59,277
Thank you so much for the thoughtful present

24
00:02:59,277 --> 00:03:01,357
Crap, it didn't work

25
00:03:01,357 --> 00:03:04,557
I wonder how she'll respond to a little bitterness

26
00:03:04,557 --> 00:03:06,377
You're so sweet

27
00:03:06,377 --> 00:03:11,677
Guess I'm the only one who thinks it's gross

28
00:03:11,677 --> 00:03:15,057
What about our neighbor's scary dog?

29
00:03:17,877 --> 00:03:20,857
Mom, I'm the only one who finds something to fight

30
00:03:20,857 --> 00:03:24,417
If I want to be the greatest mage one day

31
00:03:24,417 --> 00:03:27,397
I have to have ultimate control over my familiar

32
00:03:27,397 --> 00:03:29,617
I'm sorry

33
00:03:29,617 --> 00:03:33,997
You want to know Luco has weaknesses?

34
00:03:34,617 --> 00:03:35,077
Yeah

35
00:03:35,077 --> 00:03:37,717
Oh, I know, I've got something good

36
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:38,617
Tell me, tell me

37
00:03:38,617 --> 00:03:40,437
Those flesh orbs slow her down

38
00:03:40,437 --> 00:03:43,097
It's way too hard to dodge attacks with those things

39
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:44,557
I don't think I've got weaknesses

40
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:47,617
Okay, then, I'd say it's liquor

41
00:03:47,617 --> 00:03:48,617
Liquor?

42
00:03:48,997 --> 00:03:51,877
I thought she prided herself on how well she could hold her liquor

43
00:03:51,877 --> 00:03:53,577
Well, of course she can

44
00:03:53,577 --> 00:03:54,757
But that's not what I mean

45
00:03:54,757 --> 00:03:58,257
I'm saying she won't resist any alcohol that's put in front of her

46
00:03:58,257 --> 00:04:00,697
She's usually overly cautious about everything

47
00:04:00,697 --> 00:04:02,457
Except when it comes to throwing them back

48
00:04:02,457 --> 00:04:05,257
You could poison a drink and she'd chug it down

49
00:04:05,257 --> 00:04:07,057
I'm not trying to kill her!

50
00:04:07,157 --> 00:04:08,557
You're asking about weaknesses

51
00:04:08,557 --> 00:04:10,797
But from any dragon's perspective

52
00:04:10,797 --> 00:04:12,417
Humans are nothing but weaknesses

53
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:14,817
Even if you manage to find something

54
00:04:14,817 --> 00:04:17,477
Do you really think it would be enough to keep Lucoa at bay?

55
00:04:17,697 --> 00:04:19,697
I thought the two of you were doing well

56
00:04:19,697 --> 00:04:21,937
No, we're not

57
00:04:21,937 --> 00:04:23,317
I'm not

58
00:04:23,317 --> 00:04:26,697
Lucoa's always wandering around somewhere without telling me

59
00:04:26,697 --> 00:04:28,737
If she's here, she's teasing me

60
00:04:28,737 --> 00:04:30,097
Or making fun of me

61
00:04:30,097 --> 00:04:31,977
She just doesn't respect me at all

62
00:04:31,977 --> 00:04:34,577
I want to find some kind of weakness of hers

63
00:04:34,577 --> 00:04:36,597
So she'll remember I'm the one in charge

64
00:04:36,597 --> 00:04:39,977
I'm pretty sure she knows that already in her own way

65
00:04:39,977 --> 00:04:44,657
Lucoa's one of those dragons that can't stay in one place for very long

66
00:04:44,657 --> 00:04:47,877
If she's still with you, it's because she likes you

67
00:04:47,877 --> 00:04:49,197
Shout to sweetie

68
00:04:49,197 --> 00:04:51,657
There you are

69
00:04:51,657 --> 00:04:53,257
How long have you been here?

70
00:04:53,617 --> 00:04:55,317
Actually, I just arrived

71
00:04:55,317 --> 00:04:59,277
I want to go home

72
00:04:59,277 --> 00:05:02,777
Wait, I'll escort you

73
00:05:02,777 --> 00:05:03,997
See you later

74
00:05:03,997 --> 00:05:12,257
You know, kid

75
00:05:12,257 --> 00:05:15,297
I would have told you my weakness if you had just asked

76
00:05:15,297 --> 00:05:21,017
The thought that truly terrifies me the most is having my home taken away

77
00:05:21,017 --> 00:05:24,097
I once made a huge mistake, you know?

78
00:05:24,097 --> 00:05:26,557
And I was driven out of my homeland

79
00:05:26,557 --> 00:05:28,477
It really broke me down

80
00:05:28,477 --> 00:05:32,677
Ever since then, I've been afraid of settling in one place

81
00:05:32,677 --> 00:05:38,357
One day, a friend who I thought would never have a home found one for herself somehow

82
00:05:38,357 --> 00:05:41,697
I admit, I admit, it made me kind of jealous

83
00:05:41,697 --> 00:05:44,157
And that's why you came to me

84
00:05:44,157 --> 00:05:45,617
But why me?

85
00:05:45,617 --> 00:05:47,997
Because you're the one who invited me in

86
00:05:47,997 --> 00:05:50,177
You're the first one to ask me to stay

87
00:05:50,177 --> 00:05:53,277
I can't tell you how happy it made me to hear that

88
00:05:53,277 --> 00:05:56,237
Yeah, but I asked you as a familiar

89
00:05:56,237 --> 00:05:59,897
Honestly, I know I'm not a good match

90
00:05:59,897 --> 00:06:02,257
You're incredible at what you do

91
00:06:02,257 --> 00:06:05,217
And I'm not nearly experienced enough yet

92
00:06:05,217 --> 00:06:06,457
That's true

93
00:06:06,457 --> 00:06:09,457
I'm a phenomenal familiar

94
00:06:09,457 --> 00:06:12,117
Which is why I could read you at first glance

95
00:06:12,117 --> 00:06:16,677
You're a good boy with a kind heart who works hard

96
00:06:16,677 --> 00:06:19,437
Even to the point of overextending yourself

97
00:06:19,437 --> 00:06:21,717
Seeing that was good enough for me

98
00:06:21,717 --> 00:06:23,637
Thank you

99
00:06:23,637 --> 00:06:27,137
Such a cutie

100
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:28,977
Whatever

101
00:06:28,977 --> 00:06:32,757
I really wish she'd stop treating me like a helpless infant

102
00:06:32,757 --> 00:06:37,897
All yours, Jota

103
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:40,437
Let me know whenever you want it, okay?

104
00:06:42,577 --> 00:06:44,237
What do you mean by that?

105
00:06:47,197 --> 00:06:48,337
Wow, what's wrong?

106
00:06:48,677 --> 00:06:50,537
That was quite the dramatic sigh

107
00:06:50,537 --> 00:06:53,417
Well, my parents are coming to visit me

108
00:06:53,417 --> 00:06:54,337
Oh

109
00:06:54,337 --> 00:06:56,217
What are you going to do about Fafnir?

110
00:06:56,797 --> 00:06:57,257
Hmm

111
00:06:57,257 --> 00:07:01,677
I asked if he'd like to go adventuring in the mountains or something while they're here, but

112
00:07:01,677 --> 00:07:04,457
I absolutely refuse

113
00:07:04,457 --> 00:07:08,657
Apparently there's a brand new hardcore video game releasing at the same time, so

114
00:07:08,657 --> 00:07:11,157
I guess you'll just have to introduce them

115
00:07:11,157 --> 00:07:11,937
Right

116
00:07:11,937 --> 00:07:14,277
Both of my parents are pretty forward

117
00:07:14,277 --> 00:07:18,617
So the thought of them upsetting Fafnir and watching my treasures get half destroyed is just

118
00:07:18,617 --> 00:07:21,497
You're worried about your weeb collection?

119
00:07:21,497 --> 00:07:22,497
I refuse

120
00:07:22,497 --> 00:07:23,497
I refuse

121
00:07:23,497 --> 00:07:25,497
I can't afford to move from this spot

122
00:07:25,497 --> 00:07:27,497
Not until I've gathered all trophies

123
00:07:27,497 --> 00:07:29,257
You're pretty invested

124
00:07:29,257 --> 00:07:32,377
I mean, you've already beaten the game

125
00:07:32,377 --> 00:07:35,197
Why not reward yourself with a little time off?

126
00:07:35,197 --> 00:07:38,317
Dragons can fight off their enemies for thousands of years

127
00:07:38,317 --> 00:07:40,977
You don't need to worry about me

128
00:07:40,977 --> 00:07:44,377
Another bust

129
00:07:44,377 --> 00:07:46,237
Well, that's that

130
00:07:46,237 --> 00:07:48,057
What do I do now?

131
00:07:48,937 --> 00:07:49,257
Hmm

132
00:07:49,257 --> 00:07:52,477
Hang on

133
00:07:52,477 --> 00:07:54,657
Really?

134
00:07:54,957 --> 00:07:57,197
You're having trouble getting Fafnir to listen to you?

135
00:07:58,057 --> 00:08:01,197
Yeah, I figured you might have some pointers since you've known him the longest

136
00:08:01,197 --> 00:08:02,677
Perhaps

137
00:08:02,677 --> 00:08:06,197
I suppose I do owe you for planning that hot springs trip for us

138
00:08:06,197 --> 00:08:08,077
Thank you, Toru

139
00:08:08,077 --> 00:08:10,237
So what would you suggest that I try?

140
00:08:10,237 --> 00:08:11,377
Use Brick Fars!

141
00:08:11,637 --> 00:08:13,717
Give him no choice but to obey your commands!

142
00:08:13,717 --> 00:08:15,717
Force is your only way in!

143
00:08:15,717 --> 00:08:16,717
With Fafnir?

144
00:08:16,717 --> 00:08:17,717
Use Force?

145
00:08:17,717 --> 00:08:20,717
You know that's impossible, right?

146
00:08:20,717 --> 00:08:21,717
Not really

147
00:08:21,717 --> 00:08:24,717
It's the only method I've ever used with him

148
00:08:24,717 --> 00:08:29,717
When we first met, he attacked me for trying to sleep in his cavern and we battled

149
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:34,717
Not bad

150
00:08:34,717 --> 00:08:36,717
You're quite skilled as well

151
00:08:36,717 --> 00:08:41,717
Once we recognized each other's strength, he finally decided to share space in his big cave with me

152
00:08:41,717 --> 00:08:44,717
Wow, pretty intense for a first meeting

153
00:08:44,717 --> 00:08:48,717
I realize that method might be a bit much for a human to take on right away

154
00:08:48,717 --> 00:08:49,717
Maybe ask Lukawa?

155
00:08:49,717 --> 00:08:51,717
You really think she can help?

156
00:08:51,717 --> 00:08:52,717
Okay, what's her number?

157
00:08:52,717 --> 00:08:54,717
Hana, knock it off!

158
00:08:54,717 --> 00:08:56,717
And she hung up on me

159
00:08:56,717 --> 00:09:00,717
Who do I know who knows Lukawa?

160
00:09:00,717 --> 00:09:01,717
Oh!

161
00:09:01,717 --> 00:09:05,717
I added Shota to my friends list the last time we played games together

162
00:09:05,717 --> 00:09:10,717
What? You're here for Lukawa?

163
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:13,717
She said she was going abroad for fun

164
00:09:13,717 --> 00:09:14,717
She's not around

165
00:09:14,717 --> 00:09:15,717
Dang it

166
00:09:15,717 --> 00:09:18,717
Wait, do you need help with something?

167
00:09:18,717 --> 00:09:20,717
If so, I'd be happy to assist if I can

168
00:09:20,717 --> 00:09:21,717
You mean that?

169
00:09:21,717 --> 00:09:22,717
Yup

170
00:09:22,717 --> 00:09:26,717
I'm constantly working to improve my skills as a mage every single day

171
00:09:26,717 --> 00:09:29,717
Helping others would serve as a part of my training

172
00:09:29,717 --> 00:09:32,717
Oh wow, you're a very responsible young lad

173
00:09:32,717 --> 00:09:34,717
Here's the sitch

174
00:09:34,717 --> 00:09:36,717
That's impossible!

175
00:09:36,717 --> 00:09:39,717
You're, uh, talking about that scary dragon?

176
00:09:39,717 --> 00:09:42,717
Yeah, I guess that's what he is

177
00:09:42,717 --> 00:09:46,717
I'm thinking it might be easier to do something about my parents than Fafkun

178
00:09:46,717 --> 00:09:49,717
Huh? Who's Fafkun? The dragon?

179
00:09:49,717 --> 00:09:51,717
I thought his name was Fafnir

180
00:09:51,717 --> 00:09:53,717
Is Fafkun his nickname or something?

181
00:09:53,717 --> 00:09:56,717
What? Hmm, yeah, it is

182
00:09:56,717 --> 00:09:59,717
He's accepted that nickname as a special gift from you?

183
00:09:59,717 --> 00:10:02,717
I don't know about that, but he's fine with it

184
00:10:03,717 --> 00:10:05,717
Then you can form a pact

185
00:10:05,717 --> 00:10:06,717
What do you mean?

186
00:10:06,717 --> 00:10:09,717
If you've given him a special name, and he's accepted it

187
00:10:09,717 --> 00:10:12,717
Then the preparations to form a pact are nearly complete

188
00:10:15,717 --> 00:10:16,717
Take this

189
00:10:16,717 --> 00:10:17,717
What is it?

190
00:10:17,717 --> 00:10:19,717
An orb of magic power

191
00:10:19,717 --> 00:10:22,717
I've poured my own magical powers into it

192
00:10:22,717 --> 00:10:25,717
That should be enough for someone who doesn't have abilities to use it

193
00:10:25,717 --> 00:10:29,717
You should at least be able to activate the ritual to forge a pact

194
00:10:29,717 --> 00:10:30,717
Really?

195
00:10:30,717 --> 00:10:32,717
You're incredible, Shota

196
00:10:32,717 --> 00:10:34,717
Well, um, maybe not

197
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:37,717
Would it be okay to ask you for a favor in return?

198
00:10:37,717 --> 00:10:38,717
Oh, sure

199
00:10:38,717 --> 00:10:40,717
Like some life force?

200
00:10:40,717 --> 00:10:42,717
Only devils ask for that

201
00:10:43,717 --> 00:10:47,717
I was hoping I could convince you to exchange a lesson or two for my services

202
00:10:47,717 --> 00:10:49,717
I wanna be a cool adult too

203
00:10:49,717 --> 00:10:50,717
What?

204
00:10:50,717 --> 00:10:52,717
That's a pretty ambitious request, kid

205
00:10:52,717 --> 00:10:54,717
I'm not right for the job

206
00:10:54,717 --> 00:10:56,717
I don't know anything about being cool

207
00:10:56,717 --> 00:10:58,717
So it's a promise then

208
00:11:02,717 --> 00:11:03,717
We're making a pact

209
00:11:03,717 --> 00:11:04,717
Huh

210
00:11:05,717 --> 00:11:06,717
I'm home

211
00:11:10,717 --> 00:11:12,717
A master-servant pact

212
00:11:12,717 --> 00:11:13,717
Wow

213
00:11:13,717 --> 00:11:16,717
Fafkun

214
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:17,717
Fafkun

215
00:11:17,717 --> 00:11:18,717
Hmm?

216
00:11:18,717 --> 00:11:19,717
This is for you

217
00:11:22,717 --> 00:11:23,717
What?

218
00:11:23,717 --> 00:11:25,717
An orb of magic power?

219
00:11:25,717 --> 00:11:27,717
You think this'll do the trick?

220
00:11:27,717 --> 00:11:28,717
Oh

221
00:11:30,717 --> 00:11:31,717
I'm still not leaving

222
00:11:32,717 --> 00:11:34,717
Fine, it's a bust then

223
00:11:34,717 --> 00:11:36,717
Riddle me this, Fafkun

224
00:11:36,717 --> 00:11:38,717
How is it that someone as prideful as you

225
00:11:38,717 --> 00:11:40,717
Was able to accept a nickname from me?

226
00:11:41,717 --> 00:11:43,717
I had no idea you were taking a risk with that

227
00:11:44,717 --> 00:11:45,717
I see

228
00:11:47,717 --> 00:11:51,717
Hm, I suggest you be grateful to whichever brat gave you that measly orb

229
00:11:51,717 --> 00:11:55,717
He gave it to me in exchange for some advice on being a suave adult

230
00:11:56,717 --> 00:11:57,717
An adult? Huh

231
00:11:58,717 --> 00:12:01,717
What do you think the term adult means to a dragon?

232
00:12:01,717 --> 00:12:05,717
Um, well, it means they've matured out of their immature state

233
00:12:05,717 --> 00:12:06,717
It does not

234
00:12:06,717 --> 00:12:08,717
That only refers to the physical state of the body

235
00:12:09,717 --> 00:12:12,717
There is no concept of adult or child in a dragon's mind

236
00:12:13,717 --> 00:12:16,717
We can only track our growth in life by strength

237
00:12:18,717 --> 00:12:20,717
Our state of mind is dependent upon that

238
00:12:21,717 --> 00:12:23,717
Parents don't protect their offspring

239
00:12:24,717 --> 00:12:29,717
Dragons never used terms like adult or child until more and more of us started interacting with humans

240
00:12:30,717 --> 00:12:32,717
Do you understand? Takya?

241
00:12:32,717 --> 00:12:33,717
Takya?

242
00:12:33,717 --> 00:12:36,717
It means dragons are living their lives like humans

243
00:12:37,717 --> 00:12:40,717
They know such values will lead to nothing but foolishness

244
00:12:41,717 --> 00:12:42,717
But abide by them anyway

245
00:12:43,717 --> 00:12:45,717
The dragons here act the same

246
00:12:48,717 --> 00:12:50,717
We're all masquerading as humans

247
00:12:51,717 --> 00:12:53,717
Okay, I can tell you don't really believe that

248
00:12:54,717 --> 00:12:55,717
I hear it in your voice

249
00:12:55,717 --> 00:12:56,717
Yes

250
00:12:58,717 --> 00:12:59,717
I do

251
00:13:01,717 --> 00:13:04,717
Toru has firmly declared she will never regret her reckless decisions

252
00:13:05,717 --> 00:13:08,717
And that human, Kobayashi, drove away the Emperor of Demise

253
00:13:09,717 --> 00:13:12,717
I grew curious as to why they would go so far to keep up the act

254
00:13:13,717 --> 00:13:17,717
So I decided to try playing the human game myself to learn a bit more

255
00:13:18,717 --> 00:13:20,717
That's the only reason I'd let you give me a nickname

256
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:25,717
At long last it dropped

257
00:13:26,717 --> 00:13:28,717
This is fantastic news

258
00:13:29,717 --> 00:13:35,717
Takya, I'm in a good mood now so if you can defeat me I'll play along with your family visitors or whoever they are

259
00:13:36,717 --> 00:13:37,717
Yeah?

260
00:13:38,717 --> 00:13:39,717
I could never defeat you with strength though

261
00:13:40,717 --> 00:13:41,717
Who said it had to be physical?

262
00:13:44,717 --> 00:13:45,717
There's no way I'm gonna lose this

263
00:13:46,717 --> 00:13:47,717
You dare to challenge me, human?

264
00:13:48,717 --> 00:13:49,717
You'll never defeat me no matter how hard you try

265
00:13:50,717 --> 00:13:52,717
Hey, no fair, you can't use insta-kill combos

266
00:13:53,717 --> 00:13:55,717
We humans have no choice, we'll use any means necessary

267
00:13:55,717 --> 00:14:04,717
You assume I'm cool enough to teach you something based on my neat outwardly appearance

268
00:14:05,717 --> 00:14:09,717
That means being a cool guy starts with creating your own individual look

269
00:14:09,717 --> 00:14:23,717
Just the other day, I went as far as where the rivers meet by myself

270
00:14:24,717 --> 00:14:27,717
I guess if that's true then you are worthy of praise my friend

271
00:14:28,717 --> 00:14:30,717
